From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:46:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/55] wayland: let clients keep toplevels out of window lists
 and above others

Wayland has no way for a client to ask that a toplevel stay out of the
taskbar and window switcher, or stay above other windows, which palettes,
launchers and tray popups rely on elsewhere. kestrel_window_v1 gives each
xdg_toplevel a window state object whose requests hide the window from
window lists and keep it above, using the same window state as the
compositor's own controls. The state survives the toplevel being unmapped
and mapped again, and destroying the object undoes what it asked for.

Sandboxed clients do not see the global, so a sandboxed app cannot hide
a window from the taskbar or keep it over others.

Upstream-Status: luft-only Kestrel's private kestrel_window_v1 protocol
